---
// /disclaimer - the visible non-endorsement and accuracy surface.
//
// Riot's policies require the non-endorsement notice to be visible to users
// rather than buried in a footer, so this page leads with it: the notice is the
// first paragraph a reader meets, before any caveat about the numbers.
//
// The trademark and non-endorsement sentences come from web/src/lib/legal.ts,
// which carries the wording docs/compliance.md freezes, so this page, the footer
// on every other page and the automated gate in scripts/compliance-check.sh all
// read the same string and cannot drift apart.

import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '../layouts/JsonLd.astro';
import { integer, utcStamp, windowLabel } from '../lib/format';
import { patchLabel, snapshot } from '../lib/page';
import { absoluteUrl, jsonLdWebPage } from '../lib/seo';
import { DEMO_SOURCE, PREVIEW_TEXT } from '../lib/site';
import {
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  CONTACT_ROUTE,
  NO_RATING_TEXT,
  NON_ENDORSEMENT_TEXT,
  NOT_AFFILIATED_TEXT,
  SITE_NAME,
  TRADEMARK_TEXT,
  VERSION_LINE,
  riotVerificationNote,
} from '../lib/legal';

const snap = snapshot();
const site = snap.site;
const partition = snap.partition;
const url = absoluteUrl('/disclaimer/', Astro.site, Astro.url);
const title = `Disclaimer - ${SITE_NAME}`;
const description =
  `Non-endorsement and accuracy disclaimer for ${SITE_NAME}: an unofficial League of Legends statistics project, ` +
  'not endorsed by Riot Games and not a source of official or betting-usable figures.';

const preview = site.state === 'demo';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  patch={patchLabel(snap)}
  canonical="/disclaimer/"
  generatedAt={snap.generatedAt}
  active="/disclaimer"
>
  <JsonLd value={jsonLdWebPage(url, title, description)} />

  <article>
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>

    <p>
      <strong>{NOT_AFFILIATED_TEXT}</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>{NON_ENDORSEMENT_TEXT}</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is an unofficial fan-made statistics project. Riot Games has not reviewed, approved, sponsored or
      endorsed it, has not granted it a production API key, and is not responsible for anything it publishes. Nothing
      here is a statement by Riot Games about a champion, a role, a player or the state of the game.
    </p>

    {
      preview ? (
        <p>
          <strong>This build is a preview.</strong>{' '}
          {`${PREVIEW_TEXT}. Its numbers are generated to exercise the layout and must not be quoted, cited or ` +
            `compared as League of Legends match statistics. The manifest for this build declares its source as ` +
            `${DEMO_SOURCE}, which is how this page knows to say so.`}
        </p>
      ) : null
    }

    <h2>Unofficial statistics</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not an official source of League of Legends data and is not connected to Riot Games, its affiliates
      or anyone officially involved in producing or managing Riot Games properties. {NO_RATING_TEXT} Nothing here should
      be treated as a ranking of players, a measurement of anyone's skill, or a prediction of a match.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy and limits</h2>
    <p>
      The figures are aggregates of a sample of ranked matches, not a census of all matches played. Each rate is
      published with the number of games behind it and with a 95% confidence half-width, because a rate over a thin
      sample is not a fact about the game. Cells whose sample falls below the publication threshold are withheld rather
      than estimated, so a blank is a refusal to guess rather than a zero.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Some champions and roles are missing figures entirely, and that is a deliberate gap rather than an oversight: the
        cell did not reach the sample threshold in the snapshot behind the page you are reading.
      </li>
      <li>
        A champion's win rate moves during a patch. An early-patch reading and a late-patch reading of the same patch are
        different datasets, and neither is "the" win rate.
      </li>
      <li>
        Bracket figures are approximate stratification, because the rank a player held in each match is not part of the
        match record an aggregator receives.
      </li>
      <li>
        Percentages are rounded for presentation and the counts beside them are the authoritative part of the page: a
        difference of a tenth of a percentage point between two champions is usually sampling noise.
      </li>
    </ul>
    {
      partition ? (
        <ul>
          <li>
            Snapshot: patch {partition.patch}, region {partition.region}, queue {partition.queue}, bracket{' '}
            {partition.bracket}, crawl window{' '}
            {windowLabel(partition.source_window.from, partition.source_window.to)}, generated{' '}
            {utcStamp(partition.generated_at)}.
          </li>
          <li>
            Rank attribution is a snapshot, not a per-match fact: a bracket reflects where the accounts in the crawled
            population were seen, not the rank of every player in every game. Treat bracket figures as approximate
            stratification.
          </li>
          <li>
            A page describes the patch it was rendered for. Later patches are separate pages and are not back-filled into
            earlier ones.
          </li>
          <li>
            {integer(partition.suppressed_cells)} cells in this snapshot were withheld for being below n ={' '}
            {integer(partition.min_cell_n)} games.
          </li>
        </ul>
      ) : (
        <p>
          Nothing is published yet, so there are no figures to disclaim. The disclaimers above apply regardless.
        </p>
      )
    }

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site and its figures are provided as is, without warranty of any kind, express or implied. No promise is made
      that a page is accurate, complete, current, available or fit for any particular purpose. To the fullest extent
      permitted by the law that applies to you, the operator accepts no liability for loss or damage arising from your
      use of this site or your reliance on a figure it publishes - see clause 6 of the{' '}
      <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>. Nothing in this notice excludes any liability that cannot lawfully be
      excluded, and your mandatory consumer rights are unaffected.
    </p>

    <h2>Not advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on this site is advice about how to play, what to buy, or where to place a bet. Do not use these pages to
      make gambling decisions: the samples are partial, the intervals are wide, and the game changes with every patch. If
      a figure is tempting to treat as a certainty, look at the count behind it first; that is what the count is there
      for.
    </p>

    <h2>Assets</h2>
    <p>
      Champion, item, rune and spell icons come from Riot's Data Dragon static data and are loaded by your browser from
      Riot's own CDN. No champion art, splash art, loading screen, logo, badge or other Riot mark is hosted here,
      re-encoded here or claimed as this project's own, and no Riot asset is used to imply that Riot approves of this
      site. The names Riot Games, League of Legends and the champion and item names are used only to identify the game
      and its content, which is what they are for.
    </p>

    <h2>Riot's verified-site requirement</h2>
    <p>{riotVerificationNote()}</p>

    <h2>Report a mistake</h2>
    <p>
      {CONTACT_ROUTE} Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> if a figure is wrong, if a page
      misstates where its data came from, or if you believe something here should not be published. A correction is a new
      snapshot with its own build record rather than a quiet edit.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>{VERSION_LINE}</strong>
    </p>

    <p>
      See also the <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>, the <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and{' '}
      <a href="/about">how the numbers are produced</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
